# HRM UI — Satyakabir reference

All CMS HRM pages must match visual and layout patterns from **`HRM Satyakabir/Frontend/`** (not generic CMS portal hero cards).

## Reference source

- Layout primitives: `Frontend/src/components/app/PageHeader.tsx`, `KpiCard.tsx`, `StatStrip.tsx`, `DataExplorer.tsx`
- Page examples: `Frontend/src/routes/calendar.tsx`, `Frontend/src/components/policies/PolicyLibraryView.tsx`, `Frontend/src/routes/documents.tsx`, `Frontend/src/routes/audit.tsx`
- Analysis: `HRM Satyakabir/FRONTEND_FULL_CODE_ANALYSIS.txt`

## Required CMS kit

Import from `@/modules/hrm/hrm-reference-kit` (or `@/modules/hrm/components` re-exports):

| Pattern | Component |
|---------|-----------|
| Page title + subtitle + actions | `HrmRefPageHeader` via `HrmPageHero` |
| Count subtitle | `hrmRefCountSubtitle(n, "policy")` |
| Refresh button | `HrmRefRefreshButton` |
| KPI / stat row | `HrmRefStatStrip` via `HrmPageKpiRow` |
| Master-detail (policies, documents) | `HrmRefMasterDetail`, `HrmRefListItemContent`, `HrmRefDetailHeader` |
| Detail fields | `HrmRefDetailRow`, `HrmRefDetailSection`, `HrmRefStatusPill` |
| PDF preview / empty | `HrmRefPdfPanel` |
| Empty states | `HrmRefEmptyState` |

## Page structure

```
HrmPageShell
  HrmPageHero (Satyakabir plain header — no DashboardHero card)
  HrmPageKpiRow (gradient StatStrip chips)
  [filters / tabs if needed]
  PortalTablePanel + AdvancedTable  OR  HrmRefMasterDetail
```

## Master-detail pages

Use `HrmRefMasterDetail` with:
- Left: uppercase list label, `border-r-4 border-r-primary` on active row, icon + title + category
- Right: detail header with Edit/Delete, PDF panel or field sections

Examples: Policies, Documents, Calendar (grid + day panel).

## Table pages

Attendance, Leave, Employees, Audit, Recruitment:
- `HrmRefPageHeader` title + dynamic count subtitle
- `HrmRefRefreshButton` in actions
- Primary action: `portalActionButtonClass()` purple button with icon
- `HrmPageKpiRow` stat strip above table
- `PortalTablePanel` + `AdvancedTable` (not legacy HrmTableCard)

## Do not use on HRM pages

- `DashboardHero` motion card (CMS Companies style) — HRM uses Satyakabir plain headers
- `HrmTableCard` / `HrmAdvancedTable` — removed; use PortalTablePanel
- Placeholder-only pages without real layout when API exists

## Self-service ("My") pages

Same header + stat strip; read-only where Satyakabir employee views are read-only (e.g. My Holidays calendar).
